[{:db/id 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119623 :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/53/53e17b54ff077d45401bdc4754ccdcff5d0cad20e8d5b477b7a9e0aec37ab52c.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-89126de9-6477-52ae-9bf6-a1ac2a8f4680" "question-3276f9dc-0fc5-5be4-8351-1b5347481225"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119624 :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/c8/c85268d7db6efb171da25432988c0ee99252f4cdb10f8a1cc24f31af5b2e239d.svg) and the vector ![](images/c7/c7095b22e7a8cbbeefc6b75b63886550a4c7c35f23585e2c0006ddf14b424c28.svg) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" "question-f53050dc-6a1d-553b-afc7-7c5bd1dcb5bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119625 :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/17/17cd2f2b0846461e1ed6480f82ce576fc82e5066258d80ed6f7084b0d55ca4a9.svg) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](images/db/db533ede6312d49204e619379dfff639c0871f37ee997ce152ec35bd64105926.svg) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d" :question/id #uuid "840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74858" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc" :answer-field/id #uuid "e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" "answer-4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" "answer-43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" "answer-aac34498-7b04-5d6d-ae12-08f353104028" "answer-0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" :answer/id #uuid "1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" :answer/id #uuid "4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" :answer/id #uuid "43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{1}$,  ${b}_{2}$, and ${b}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aac34498-7b04-5d6d-ae12-08f353104028" :answer/id #uuid "aac34498-7b04-5d6d-ae12-08f353104028" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/id #uuid "0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-89126de9-6477-52ae-9bf6-a1ac2a8f4680" :question/id #uuid "89126de9-6477-52ae-9bf6-a1ac2a8f4680" :question/math-academy-id "q-111103" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2k-6 \\\\ -k+3 \\\\ 4k-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ -k+3=0 \\\\ 4k-12=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b31ab65-a8d2-52bf-9fe7-84343a8c24b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b31ab65-a8d2-52bf-9fe7-84343a8c24b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b31ab65-a8d2-52bf-9fe7-84343a8c24b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59f64036-7331-5cd3-843e-78a74738a9d7" "answer-a602ff6b-6d7d-5c41-a3a4-a43d6175780c" "answer-d5fab15a-6aaa-5d52-a720-35f24b947f9a" "answer-754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" "answer-4345a24b-01f2-51a9-a9a3-ec26cb12faf8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59f64036-7331-5cd3-843e-78a74738a9d7" :answer/id #uuid "59f64036-7331-5cd3-843e-78a74738a9d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a602ff6b-6d7d-5c41-a3a4-a43d6175780c" :answer/id #uuid "a602ff6b-6d7d-5c41-a3a4-a43d6175780c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5fab15a-6aaa-5d52-a720-35f24b947f9a" :answer/id #uuid "d5fab15a-6aaa-5d52-a720-35f24b947f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" :answer/id #uuid "754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4345a24b-01f2-51a9-a9a3-ec26cb12faf8" :answer/id #uuid "4345a24b-01f2-51a9-a9a3-ec26cb12faf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3276f9dc-0fc5-5be4-8351-1b5347481225" :question/id #uuid "3276f9dc-0fc5-5be4-8351-1b5347481225" :question/math-academy-id "q-34382" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3+k+2 \\\\ 4+2k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k+5=0 \\\\ 2k+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-035f7b17-da06-59f6-9265-6f52b45bcb1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-035f7b17-da06-59f6-9265-6f52b45bcb1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "035f7b17-da06-59f6-9265-6f52b45bcb1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" :answer-field/choices ["answer-065f9865-0513-58da-9b22-d96229767c84" "answer-c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" "answer-ae95c44a-5b3c-5f86-ad5d-103a70a2b3df" "answer-2ecdee28-7a39-54e8-b845-add658821807" "answer-2bc79277-ae90-5b10-b515-d4f65951b373"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-065f9865-0513-58da-9b22-d96229767c84" :answer/id #uuid "065f9865-0513-58da-9b22-d96229767c84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" :answer/id #uuid "c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae95c44a-5b3c-5f86-ad5d-103a70a2b3df" :answer/id #uuid "ae95c44a-5b3c-5f86-ad5d-103a70a2b3df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ecdee28-7a39-54e8-b845-add658821807" :answer/id #uuid "2ecdee28-7a39-54e8-b845-add658821807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bc79277-ae90-5b10-b515-d4f65951b373" :answer/id #uuid "2bc79277-ae90-5b10-b515-d4f65951b373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" :question/id #uuid "87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111154" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef" :answer-field/id #uuid "59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88ca81a7-6293-5d02-80a7-1fbb2af96184" "answer-29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" "answer-aa0d38bc-db7b-538c-b0be-911380152f0e" "answer-7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" "answer-8000a495-b4c4-55db-b5e6-b3a10f46cfdc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88ca81a7-6293-5d02-80a7-1fbb2af96184" :answer/id #uuid "88ca81a7-6293-5d02-80a7-1fbb2af96184" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/id #uuid "29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa0d38bc-db7b-538c-b0be-911380152f0e" :answer/id #uuid "aa0d38bc-db7b-538c-b0be-911380152f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" :answer/id #uuid "7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8000a495-b4c4-55db-b5e6-b3a10f46cfdc" :answer/id #uuid "8000a495-b4c4-55db-b5e6-b3a10f46cfdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f53050dc-6a1d-553b-afc7-7c5bd1dcb5bf" :question/id #uuid "f53050dc-6a1d-553b-afc7-7c5bd1dcb5bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-111165" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9debef96-eaa3-515c-b307-163bd264f5ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9debef96-eaa3-515c-b307-163bd264f5ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "9debef96-eaa3-515c-b307-163bd264f5ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" "answer-e3dcbb04-64eb-5c82-a9e6-1019c7c418e3" "answer-4c4607fe-b4f6-500f-b628-c9efb2f77b90" "answer-cbb639f6-eb5e-5bc1-a3ee-ebf239dfc56d" "answer-63a9c9e9-789b-5e69-a3e9-b68cbdaf3c6e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" :answer/id #uuid "267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3dcbb04-64eb-5c82-a9e6-1019c7c418e3" :answer/id #uuid "e3dcbb04-64eb-5c82-a9e6-1019c7c418e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c4607fe-b4f6-500f-b628-c9efb2f77b90" :answer/id #uuid "4c4607fe-b4f6-500f-b628-c9efb2f77b90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbb639f6-eb5e-5bc1-a3ee-ebf239dfc56d" :answer/id #uuid "cbb639f6-eb5e-5bc1-a3ee-ebf239dfc56d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63a9c9e9-789b-5e69-a3e9-b68cbdaf3c6e" :answer/id #uuid "63a9c9e9-789b-5e69-a3e9-b68cbdaf3c6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121039 :tutorial/content "The **null space** of a matrix $A$ is the set of all the solutions of the equation $A\\mathbf{x}= \\mathbf{0},$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Null}(A).$ \n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/c3/c3bf583e98daad3fa753880b96c6ba85bce697f3434690977c5679b64ffd4882.svg)\n\nThe null space consists of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ For example, the vectors ![](images/9d/9d94e47625ee3c9d6fdff788db07e925ec2375e6c57cc6c1d8897ba423749abf.svg) ![](images/e5/e5a5f6b93eccdf25da72ea39af64a4a5cca7b0a03d5f469cb85554dc6dc12f88.svg) and $[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ all satisfy the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0},$ so they are all elements of the null space:\n\n![](images/5e/5ededa27ee77302b18683f91e37d854a68cd3ba6ceacc7e2a6068a2730b4a9bf.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121063 :tutorial/content "Let's again consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/8f/8fa69630c71d5106ed04a5281681992687174891b1c0978521c12e914cb3a0b0.svg)\n\nTo find an expression for the null space using set-builder notation, we need to find all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Let's start by considering the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ and finding its reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,0] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st column). The second column is not a pivot column.\n\nNow, we convert the reduced matrix back into a system, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $\\color{blue}x_1$ is a basic variable (it corresponds to the pivot column), while $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable (it corresponds to the non-pivot column). Because there is a free variable, the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions. \n\nFrom the first equation we get ${\\color{blue}x_1}=-3{\\color{red}x_2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is\n![](images/8c/8c5541adb07cb58136d71fb4e3218981f1717b929f22acbe55d133cd0c395870.svg)\n\n**Note:** It is not necessary to consider the full augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ since the last column won't be changed during the process of reduction. Really, we just need to find the reduced row echelon form of the matrix $A$ and then set up the corresponding system." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120048 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
